================================================================================
What this is
================================================================================
NormalBake is a standalone, clean-room, managed-C# tool that bakes a normal map
from a high-resolution mesh into the UV space of a low-resolution (quad-remeshed)
mesh. No third-party source code is copied into it; the algorithms it implements
are described in the works below, and the permissively-licensed reference bakers
are used only as an offline test oracle (built/run locally to emit golden images,
never linked or redistributed).

================================================================================
Algorithmic influences and attributions (clean-room — read for understanding)
================================================================================
  J. Cohen, M. Olano, D. Manocha. "Appearance-Preserving Simplification."
  SIGGRAPH 1998. (Introduced/coined the normal map.)

  P. Cignoni, C. Montani, C. Rocchini, R. Scopigno. "A general method for
  preserving attribute values on simplified meshes." IEEE Visualization 1998.
  (The high->low attribute/normal baking algorithm a baker implements.)

  M. S. Mikkelsen. "Simulation of Wrinkled Surfaces Revisited." MSc thesis,
  University of Copenhagen, 2008. (Tangent-space standardization — MikkTSpace.)
  Reference implementation "MikkTSpace": zlib license. A clean-room C# port, if
  used, keeps the zlib notice and does not misrepresent origin.

See docs/design/references.md for the full bibliography.

================================================================================
Reference oracle (test-only; not shipped, not linked)
================================================================================
Golden normal maps are generated by Blender (GPL) running headless, with xNormal
(freeware) as a historical cross-check. These tools are invoked as external
processes to produce committed golden images; no code from them is included or
redistributed.

================================================================================
Third-party runtime dependencies
================================================================================
The core ships dependency-light. Permissively-licensed managed packages are added
per phase (docs/plans/02-phase-roadmap.md) and listed here as they land:

  BCnEncoder.NET   BC5/BC7 + DDS encode/decode  (MIT OR Unlicense)
                   (pulls CommunityToolkit.HighPerformance, MIT)

The PNG and OpenEXR writers and the OBJ/glTF/FBX readers are hand-rolled in
NormalBake.IO (no dependency); the float EXR writer fills in for Jither.OpenEXR,
which is not published on NuGet. The binary FBX reader is clean-room — it parses
the documented Kaydara/Autodesk binary record format (no Autodesk FBX SDK, no
native code); array decompression uses the framework's System.IO.Compression.

ImageSharp is deliberately avoided (Six Labors Split License) to keep the
dependency graph unconditionally permissive.
